test mv-path-last-use-copies {the natural ways to update a struct of vectors copy nothing once each read-out is the last use of its own path: a rebuild from the struct's own fields after mutating them, a result struct whose vector field is passed on before its Int field is read, the whole struct handed to a mutating call while only its Int field is read after it, and a sub-struct field rebuilt beside an Int sibling -- natively no share and no detach, and the elaboration wrote no copy} -constraints nativeCoroutines -body {
